savestates: deterministic across processes and loads

A Mega Drive state saved and loaded did not give back the same machine:

- YM2612SaveContext and the Z80 part dumped whole structs, host pointers
  included (24 slot DT pointers, 30 channel output connections, the Z80
  irq callback and daisy chain). The load path recomputes or restores
  every one of them, so they only made two states of one machine differ
  between processes, which defeats byte comparison of savestates
  (RetroArch replay checkpoints). They are cleared in the saved copy.
- state_load() calls system_reset(), which synchronizes the 68k bus
  refresh phase to the cycle count of whatever ran before the load, and
  then restores the saved cycle count without redoing it. The VDP FIFO
  read-out timestamps are neither saved nor reset. Both leaked the
  pre-load machine's timing into the loaded one; a game polling in its
  idle loop then advances its RNG differently (Thunder Force IV).

No state format change.

